1:46Z","updated_at":"2026-09-27T11:55:40Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in v4.7.stable.official\n- Not reproducible in v4.6.3.stable.official\n\n### System information\n\nmacOS - v4.7.stable.official\n\n### Issue description\n\nOpening scripts written in a ScriptLanguageExtension stopped highlight code in Godot code editor in 4.7, it used to work fine in 4.6.3. Reported in https://github.com/gilzoide/lua-gdextension/issues/242.\n\nI've traced the problem to commit 2363720b5396c6db20503a9344bfd3f6252336bf, where `EditorPlainTextSyntaxHighlighter` is the new default syntax highlighter used by `ScriptTextEditor`, set in `TextEditorBase`.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Clone https://github.com/gilzoide/lua-gdextension\n2. Open the project inside `test` folder in Godot 4.7\n3. Double-click any Lua script in the FileSystem tab\n4. Check that Lua code doesn't have syntax highlighting. If you open `test/.godot/editor/script_editor_cache.cfg` file you'll see \"Plain Text\" syntax highlighter being used for Lua scripts.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nhttps://github.com/gilzoide/lua-gdextension repository's `test` folder","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121288/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121288/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}